  "_comment": "Curated technology names, read by both the AI service (relations.py) and Next.js (skill-relations.ts). Keys and variants are written as the shared tokenizer produces them: lower case, dots removed, words separated by single spaces. A canonical name is one token. 'aliases' are the SAME technology under another name (may support a match). 'concepts' are families of RELATED technologies (at most 'possible', never 'supported'). 'distinct' pairs are never related. 'ambiguous' words are also ordinary English words: in free text they count only next to a 'tech_context' word. 'employment_words' mark an Experience requirement as being about employment rather than a technology. Changing this file changes what local AI may claim, so it needs review.",
